WEBVTT

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:10.940
<i>The Hoshinomori Summer Festival 
ended as a huge success.</i>

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:13.830
<i>However, they didn't want it to end like this.</i>

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:17.320
<i>Seeking new activities, the members of 
the Hoshi Festival executive committee</i>

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:25.420
<i>formed a new organization known 
as the Hoshigei event committee.</i>

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:25.420
<b>Hoshigei Event Committee</b>

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:30.220
<i>Their battle had just begun.</i>

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:36.580
<i>Ah, glory to the young artistas 
drawn by the Light of Arte.</i>

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:38.930
Suminomiya.

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:42.590
I can't read this committee log at all.

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:43.910
What?

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:53.110
Halloween Party

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:53.110
I'd like to suggest a Halloween party for 
the Hoshigei event committee's first job.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.940
I'm glad we decided on something.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:58.370
We sure did have a lot of ideas, though.

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:13.460
Fruit Picking
Maze?
Game of Tag—standard rules
Shops
Lantern Making
Pumpkin Roll
Haunted House
Costume Parade
Play

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:00.880
I wanted to hold a moon viewing party.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.940
It's already early September.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.470
There's not nearly enough time.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:07.300
In that case, why don't we do it ourselves?

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.380
That's an idea.

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:10.560
Rin Rin, I'd love to try your dumplings.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.390
I don't mind dumplings.

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:13.460
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.490
Let's hold a costume contest, too.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:16.880
That's a great idea.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.590
Costumes? I'm excited.

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:21.580
Are you guys trying to 
give us more work to do?

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:24.230
If we're going to do all 
of them, we need a plan.

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:25.540
You're right.

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:28.730
And the committee has its 
own performance to put on.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:28.730
<b>Play</b>

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:31.820
A play, uh? That's fine by me,

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:34.240
but can you make 
that happen all on your own?

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.100
Don't worry about us.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.770
We've called in an instructor.

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:38.980
An instructor?

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:42.770
Acting major Chikamatsu Juri-san.

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:44.450
Since it's a request from Kohana,

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:47.000
I have to do everything I can.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.380
Is everyone ready?

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.000
I'm going to train you boys real good.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:11.180
<b>Magic-Kyun Renaissance!</b>

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:25.970
You Are the Prince of Destiny

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.910
It's the Hoshi Festival News.

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:37.940
Apparently, the executive committee is back.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:41.450
<b>We're holding a Halloween Party!!</b>

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.210
They're holding a Halloween party next?

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:41.450
There are a lot of events this year.

00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:41.450
That sounds fun.

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:47.070
Once upon a time,

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:49.200
a princess fell into a long slumber

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.980
after being cursed by an evil witch.

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:56.710
There was a certain prophecy 
concerning the princess.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:04:00.320
A hundred years after falling asleep,

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:04.470
the princess' prince of destiny 
would arrive to save her.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:06.550
As of today, exactly one 
hundred years have gone by.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:10.570
Each believing that he is the one,
 six princes head for the princess.

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:13.840
Who will be her prince of destiny?

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.700
I based it on Sleeping Beauty.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:19.280
What do you think?

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:20.330
I read it.

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:21.840
It was entertaining.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:22.780
Thanks.

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:25.170
But why Sleeping Beauty?

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:27.280
Aren't pumpkins more Cinderella's thing?

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.960
Who cares about the details?

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:31.930
In any case, let's choose roles.

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:33.430
Kohana, you'll be the princess.

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:34.040
What?

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:39.300
Then, there's the prince of destiny who 
shares a kissing scene with the princess...

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.030
I'll play the prince.

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:41.950
No, I will.

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:42.800
No, me!

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:46.080
Well, it's just a pretend kiss.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:49.990
Okay, let's hold an audition.

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:50.790
An audition?

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:54.310
Yep, enthusiasm isn't enough 
to play the starring role.

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:56.440
I'm not sure that's necessary.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.800
After all, I'm going to be the prince.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:00.860
What?

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:02.570
That's not a very funny joke.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:04.440
The prince will be played by...

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:05.500
Me.

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.070
All of you?

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:10.150
Tatewaki, Anjo, Hibiki,

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:11.760
I like how assertive you are.

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:12.830
You get ten points.

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:19.080
<i>The audition has already started!</i>

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:22.590
<i>The time has finally arrived.</i>

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:27.010
<b>First Prince Showdown Final!!</b>

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:27.500
<i>The magnificent and fierce battle to 
determine who will play the prince of destiny.</i>

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:29.640
<i>I'm your running commentator, 
Chikamatsu Juri.</i>

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:32.980
<i>And analyzing the audition 
will be Aigasaki Kohana-san.</i>

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:33.970
<i>I'll do my best.</i>

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:36.340
What? A running commentator?

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:38.480
<i>First up is the 200 meter dash.</i>

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:41.480
<i>The competitors are wearing 
nervous expressions.</i>

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.990
<i>Only one of them will be crowned the winner.</i>

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:48.740
<i>Who among them will win the starring role?</i>

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:50.240
On your marks.

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:53.920
Get set...

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:02.500
<i>What's this? Tatewaki and Hibiki 
are off to a good start.</i>

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:04.130
I won't lose to you, Hibiki.

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:05.130
Neither will I.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.440
<i>It's a clash of wills.</i>

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:07.440
You can do it! You can do it!

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:09.130
<i>Neither one is giving any ground.</i>

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:10.760
<i>They're entering the straight.</i>

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:12.960
<i>They both look desperate.</i>

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:15.470
<i>I can't look away.</i>

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:16.600
I will...

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:17.600
Win!

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:24.750
<i>I don't believe it.</i>

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:27.380
<i>Ichijoji finishes first.</i>

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:28.400
<i>What a strategist.</i>

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:30.660
<i>He saved his energy until the very end.</i>

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:34.700
Juri-chan, your commentary was amazing.

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:37.880
<i>Here come the scores.</i>

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:42.130
<b>Tsukushi  Suminomiya  Anjo  Hibiki  Tatewaki  Ichijoji</b>

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:43.590
What's going on?

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:46.760
How did Anjo-senpai and 
Suminomiya-senpai score ten points each?

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:50.260
I told you, you're auditioning 
to play a prince.

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:53.140
Anjo-senpai's elegant steps.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:56.010
Suminomiya's beautiful form.

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:58.450
Their total lack of interest 
in the competition.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:00.340
They truly are princes.

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:01.440
Yeah.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:03.260
What kind of reasoning is that?!

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:04.720
This should be a serious competition!

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:07.580
Shut up already.

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:09.200
I <i>am</i> taking this seriously.

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:12.660
And can you really claim you 
gave everything you had?

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:15.260
Oh, right. Sorry.

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:16.540
How unsightly.

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:19.280
You two should just quit.

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:20.910
You only scored one point!

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.730
I was just watching.

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:25.040
Next time I won't lose.

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:27.760
Really? Let's see you do it, then.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:30.420
<i>This is a rather interesting development.</i>

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:33.050
<i>Let's move on to the next event.</i>

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:36.280
<i>Next up is a series of one-on-one battles.</i>

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:37.940
<i>No matter the adverse circumstances,</i>

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:39.680
<i>in the end, you must seize victory.</i>

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:42.480
<i>That is how a prince should be.</i>

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:44.010
You can do it, everyone.

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:46.360
I thought winning didn't matter.

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:51.200
<i>Tatewaki and Tsukushi will be 
competing in a penalty shootout.</i>

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:55.200
Rintaro, have you fixed your tell?

00:07:56.210 --> 00:07:57.450
What are you talking about?

00:07:57.690 --> 00:07:59.060
You mean you don't know?

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:01.180
Rintaro, you can tell based on your form

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:03.580
whether you're going to shoot right or left.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:04.640
What?

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:08.840
I noticed it while watching you 
play a game in middle school.

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:13.090
Seriously?

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:15.680
<i>This isn't good. Which way should I go?</i>

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:17.850
<i>Right or left?</i>

00:08:20.030 --> 00:08:21.680
<i>I know!</i>

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:24.040
<i>If he can predict if I'm 
kicking right or left,</i>

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:25.730
<i>I'll go straight down the middle!</i>

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:31.990
So simpleminded.

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:34.300
<i>Tsukushi stopped the ball!</i>

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:37.240
<i>Did Tatewaki completely play into his hands?</i>

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.450
Rintaro, it's a good thing 
you're so easy to read.

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:42.620
Damn it!

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:47.750
Next up are Anjo-senpai and Hibiki.

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:50.240
They'll be competing in an archery contest.

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:52.010
It suddenly got quiet.

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:04.200
All right, a hit.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:09.860
Impressive, Anjo-senpai—

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:10.480
What?

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:13.740
I achieved a sexy victory.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:14.990
You're taking your clothes off again!

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:17.360
Too sexy! Minus ten points!

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:19.170
What? Why?

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:21.240
Just one side would've been enough.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:23.480
One side's okay?

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:29.250
<i>Next up are Ichijoji and Suminomiya.</i>

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:33.510
<i>They're old rivals both considered 
top candidates for Artista Prince.</i>

00:09:34.060 --> 00:09:37.010
<i>This will surely be a fierce battle.</i>

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:49.730
They're both so amazing.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:51.650
Why are they playing in robes?

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:55.280
It's been a while since 
we last played together.

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:57.320
Not since grade school.

00:09:57.320 --> 00:10:00.910
Our record is 99-99.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:02.660
<i>Whoever wins next will reach 100!</i>

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:04.540
<i>The audition is important, too!</i>

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:05.680
<i>But...</i>

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:07.040
<i>This is a battle...</i>

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.290
<i>I cannot lose!</i>

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:32.860
Yes.

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:35.000
<i>Ichijoji wins.</i>

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:39.210
<i>The heated play was truly appropriate 
for such a decisive match.</i>

00:10:39.210 --> 00:10:41.110
They were only playing to one point?

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:48.500
Good game. Let's play again sometime.

00:10:49.820 --> 00:10:50.870
Yeah.

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:56.550
Ichijoji and Suminomiya.

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:58.080
One thousand points!

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:00.880
That's way too many.

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:02.980
<i>Next up is a contest of intelligence.</i>

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:04.510
<i>Buzz in first to answer.</i>

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:05.390
<i>Here's your question.</i>

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:08.140
<b>Question

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:08.140
<b>Hijiki</b>

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:08.140
<i>How do you read these kanji?</i>

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:09.280
Me.

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:10.160
<i>Hibiki.</i>

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:11.460
Shikaona.

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:13.520
<i>Wrong.</i>

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:16.360
<i>Suminomiya.</i>

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:17.780
Hijiki.

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:20.370
Way to go, Suminomiya.

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:22.610
Kanji are his specialty.

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:24.680
<i>Next question. Once—</i>

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:27.090
The island of Mauritius.

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:28.470
What?

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:29.370
How did you figure that out?

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:31.620
<i>Next question. It—</i>

00:11:31.930 --> 00:11:33.470
The Ho-o-do.

00:11:34.140 --> 00:11:34.880
<i>Correct.</i>

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:36.130
<i>Next ques—</i>

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:39.250
1984.

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:40.260
<i>Correct.</i>

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:41.880
Amazing.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:43.640
Is this really intelligence?

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:45.510
Let's keep going.

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:49.390
A prince must always possess 
the following qualities.

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:51.270
He must never shy away from danger.

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:53.310
He must rush to all places.

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:55.810
He must gracefully ride white horses.

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:57.320
At times heroic.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.820
Other times delicate.

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:00.690
Never forgetting kindness.

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:03.460
That's what it means to truly be a prince.

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:04.450
<b>Tsukushi  Suminomiya  Anjo  Hibiki  Tatewaki  Ichijoji</b>

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:07.450
I am... the prince.

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:09.960
No, I am.

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:11.080
No, me.

00:12:11.650 --> 00:12:13.460
<i>Now for the second half 
of the competition.</i>

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:16.610
<i>Aigasaki Kohana-san has 
provided the analysis so far.</i>

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:18.120
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:20.180
Thank you.

00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:22.340
I don't get a thank you?

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:26.090
<i>Next is the acting competition 
you've all been waiting for.</i>

00:12:26.670 --> 00:12:29.060
<i>You'll each perform the kissing 
scene with the princess.</i>

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:33.420
For you.

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:34.740
Magic.

00:12:34.740 --> 00:12:35.980
Kyun.

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:38.760
Magic-Kyun.

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:40.100
Renaissance.

00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:48.030
Here.

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:49.940
Thank you.

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:52.870
Is this cup your newest work?

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:55.300
Yeah, I was inspired to make something.

00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:56.960
It's wonderful.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:58.310
I still have a lot to learn.

00:12:58.310 --> 00:12:59.980
It's not worthy of any praise.

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:01.990
I wouldn't say that.

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:06.690
It's warm.

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:08.100
Yeah.

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:13.570
<i>The contest will now begin.</i>

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:17.400
<i>You'll be performing the scene in 
which the prince wakes the princess.</i>

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:20.140
<i>These stuffed animals will 
represent the princess.</i>

00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:23.150
<i>Ignore the script and pour 
your hearts out to them.</i>

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:26.280
<i>Our first challenger is...</i>

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:27.700
<i>You.</i>

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:30.780
Okay.

00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:43.150
My princess of destiny.

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:45.860
I have adored you greatly.

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:48.750
Um...

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:52.500
Your eyes, your lips.

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:55.240
Everything about you has stolen my heart.

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:06.070
Just kidding.

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:08.040
Wake up soon.

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:11.780
I promise I'll make you happy.

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:22.240
The stars are so beautiful.

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:26.680
If the two of us could dance 
until dawn in the starlight,

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:28.220
I would be so happy.

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:36.720
Princess, I'll be waiting for you to wake up.

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:37.980
Forever.

00:14:44.210 --> 00:14:46.530
I don't believe in destiny.

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:49.620
I acquire what I want with my own strength.

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:51.990
Isn't that what it means to be a man?

00:14:53.190 --> 00:14:54.150
But...

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:58.510
I'll believe in destiny today.

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:02.500
After all, I'm the one who will wake you.

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:11.400
We finally meet.

00:15:12.130 --> 00:15:14.720
They say you've been asleep 
for a hundred years.

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:16.260
What have you been dreaming about?

00:15:16.760 --> 00:15:19.090
It'd be great if you had fun dreams.

00:15:19.820 --> 00:15:23.100
But if they were sad, I'll cheer you up.

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:27.880
You've been sleeping for a hundred years
 so you could meet me.

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:32.380
So don't take your eyes off me.

00:15:32.380 --> 00:15:33.740
Okay?

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:40.060
Thank you.

00:15:40.060 --> 00:15:43.880
Thanks to you, I was able to change.

00:15:44.410 --> 00:15:49.130
I hope you'll accept my gratitude.

00:15:56.070 --> 00:15:58.570
The moon is beautiful tonight.

00:15:58.570 --> 00:16:02.140
Don't you agree?

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:10.910
I always thought that I lived in darkness.

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:18.030
But... you taught me that 
I live in the light, too.

00:16:22.490 --> 00:16:26.520
Now it's my turn to shine my light on you.

00:16:33.610 --> 00:16:35.180
You all pass.

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:38.150
All your feelings were genuine.

00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:41.740
You even met my unreasonable 
demands with sincerity.

00:16:41.740 --> 00:16:43.310
You knew what you were doing?

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:46.820
Any of you would make a fine prince.

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:47.930
I can guarantee that.

00:16:47.930 --> 00:16:49.210
Wait a minute.

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:50.480
You have to choose someone.

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:52.820
What were those competitions for, then?

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:56.160
Ah, but reality is so cruel.

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:59.980
I have to choose just one of you.

00:16:59.980 --> 00:17:01.080
Wasn't it that way from the start?

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:05.580
Why don't we let fate decide?

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:07.460
Fate?

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:12.460
The last person holding this card wins.

00:17:12.770 --> 00:17:14.340
That's just Old Maid.

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:16.090
It's not Old Maid.

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:18.400
It's Young Prince.

00:17:18.400 --> 00:17:21.100
Either way, it has nothing 
to do with their abilities.

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:23.980
Fate is a skill, too.

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:29.820
The game is coming to a close.

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:33.230
It's come down to the king 
and Tatewaki-senpai.

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:35.610
Disappointing.

00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:51.880
You're wasting your time.

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:54.830
A perfect poker face?

00:17:55.920 --> 00:17:56.630
All right.

00:17:56.920 --> 00:17:57.880
Let's go with...

00:17:57.880 --> 00:18:01.720
This one!

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:07.890
I win.

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:10.440
Damn it!

00:18:11.080 --> 00:18:12.660
It's been decided!

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:15.880
The prince of destiny will 
be played by Ichijoji Teika!

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:16.400
All right.

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:20.260
Ichijoji, I'll be trying to 
steal the spotlight from you.

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:21.530
Prepare yourself.

00:18:22.130 --> 00:18:23.280
Bring it on.

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:27.410
I'm the one who will make the 
princess shine the brightest.

00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:31.790
Really? You might be a real prince, then.

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:33.190
Okay, okay.

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:35.420
Now that we've chosen a prince of destiny,

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:36.800
let's start practicing.

00:18:37.230 --> 00:18:39.620
What about the rest of the roles?

00:18:39.620 --> 00:18:41.810
I've chosen them based on 
the audition we just held.

00:18:41.810 --> 00:18:43.920
No objections.

00:18:43.920 --> 00:18:44.810
Yeah, yeah.

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:46.780
Have you all memorized your lines?

00:18:46.780 --> 00:18:47.760
Of course.

00:18:47.760 --> 00:18:48.310
What?

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:49.970
Way to go, Suminomiya-senpai.

00:18:49.970 --> 00:18:51.170
That was quick.

00:18:51.170 --> 00:18:52.770
Yeah, right.

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:54.600
Everyone else, memorize 
your lines in ten minutes.

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:55.370
Ten minutes?

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:56.320
That's so short!

00:18:56.320 --> 00:18:58.950
But we'll just have to do it.

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:00.960
Okay, input complete.

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:01.320
I'm excited.

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:01.320
What?

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:03.120
Kanato, did you already memorize your lines?

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:04.510
I can't believe we're acting in a play together.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:05.040
Actually, I'm better at all-nighters.

00:19:04.510 --> 00:19:06.580
I'm sure something fun will happen again.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:07.120
Better? That's too fast.

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:10.100
I'd better work just as hard.

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:10.150
Calm down. What matters most is our focus.

00:19:10.100 --> 00:19:11.480
You're right.

00:19:10.150 --> 00:19:12.390
Sumi, how did you memorize your lines?

00:19:12.390 --> 00:19:13.840
Sleep learning.

00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:22.090
Sir.

00:19:22.380 --> 00:19:23.900
What do you want?

00:19:23.900 --> 00:19:25.510
What are you doing here?

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:31.100
Todo-kun, there's something 
I have to tell you.

00:19:36.850 --> 00:19:39.490
Okay, let's do a run-through.

00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:48.330
The princess is mine.

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:51.020
Heave, ho! Heave, ho! Heave, ho!

00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:53.460
Everything in this world belongs to me.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:57.460
I will remove your curse.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:01.090
I won't let you have the princess.

00:20:03.080 --> 00:20:05.350
I'll make destiny yield to me!

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:08.720
I accept your challenge.

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:15.570
That's it. Switch over right there.

00:20:15.570 --> 00:20:17.480
Good. Keep up the tension.

00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:20.430
Juri-chan's sparkles are incredible.

00:20:20.430 --> 00:20:21.990
I'd better do my best, too.

00:20:26.770 --> 00:20:28.320
Kohana, you're on.

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:29.800
Okay.

00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:46.830
You're the one who dispelled 
the curse and woke me.

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:48.760
This is for you.

00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:54.120
Thank you, my prince of destiny.

00:21:04.260 --> 00:21:05.470
Aigasaki.

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:10.030
Aigasaki!

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:10.030
Aigasaki-senpai!

00:21:10.030 --> 00:21:11.540
Kohana!

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:13.910
Are you all right, Aigasaki?

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:17.880
Good, you're awake.

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:19.120
Are you okay?

00:21:19.120 --> 00:21:23.390
Yeah. I suddenly felt dizzy.

00:21:23.390 --> 00:21:24.300
Anemia?

00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:27.090
Maybe you should go to the nurse's office.

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:29.300
I was too late.

00:21:32.880 --> 00:21:34.310
Sir?

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:37.310
What are you talking about?

00:21:37.970 --> 00:21:39.310
Aigasaki-san.

00:21:40.260 --> 00:21:41.070
Yes?

00:21:41.840 --> 00:21:43.490
I'm sorry to say this,

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:47.950
but you have to leave Hoshigei.

00:21:50.930 --> 00:21:54.100
Leave Hoshigei?

00:23:25.700 --> 00:23:28.880
Senpai's always giving us energy.

00:23:28.880 --> 00:23:32.090
It'd be great if we could 
make her smile this time.

00:23:32.090 --> 00:23:32.720
Yeah.

00:23:32.940 --> 00:23:34.850
Next time on Magic-Kyun! Renaissance:

00:23:34.850 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>The Sleeping Princess 
of the Frozen Forest</b>

00:23:35.200 --> 00:23:37.380
"The Sleeping Princess of the Frozen Forest."

00:23:37.380 --> 00:23:38.480
For all you hard workers.

00:23:38.480 --> 00:23:39.980
Magic-Kyun!
